---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Motif from "../components/Motif.astro";

// People who transcribed Morais's writings and correspondence.
const transcribers = [
  { name: "Alessia Fontanella", role: "PhD student, Bar-Ilan University" },
  { name: "Alice Avanzi", role: "Independent researcher" },
  { name: "Camilla Berveglieri", role: "Master's student, Venice" },
  { name: "Donatella Fischer", role: "Independent researcher" },
  { name: "Martina Perotta", role: "PhD student, Trento" },
  { name: "Pia Settimi", role: "Independent researcher" },
  { name: "Martina Mampieri", role: "" },
];

// FromThePage volunteers who transcribed/reviewed; credited by username
// because we don't have their real names.
const reviewers = [
  "LIFrancophone",
  "sabern",
  "AFontanella",
  "Alice A.T.",
  "MaryV",
  "glnite",
  "Steviedog",
  "sofiaglynne",
  "txblaize",
];

const partners = [
  "Penn Libraries",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acknowledgements"
  description="The people, institutions, and funders behind the Sabato Morais Digital Repository."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">With Gratitude</p>
      <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl leading-tight text-navy sm:text-5xl">
        Acknowledgements
      </h1>
      <div class="ornament mx-auto mt-6 max-w-sm">
        <Motif class="text-gold" size={20} />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none font-body text-lg text-ink prose-headings:font-heading prose-headings:text-navy prose-a:text-burgundy prose-strong:text-ink">
      <p>
        The <strong>Sabato Morais Digital Repository</strong> is the work of many
        hands. We are grateful to the individuals and institutions whose scholarship,
        care, and generosity made this collection possible.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Morais Ledger & the Weiner family -->
    <div class="mt-12">
      <section class="frame-gold rounded-sm bg-card p-7 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="mb-6 font-heading text-2xl text-navy">The Morais Ledger &amp; the Weiner Family</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none font-body text-lg text-ink prose-a:text-burgundy prose-strong:text-ink">
          <p>
            The Sabato Morais Ledger, housed with the Sabato Morais Papers (ARC MS8)
            at the Library at the Herbert D. Katz Center for Advanced Judaic Studies,
            University of Pennsylvania, has been conserved, microfilmed, and digitized
            thanks to a preservation grant award from the National Foundation for
            Jewish Culture. It may be viewed online at{" "}
            <a href="https://judaicadh.github.io/morais-ledger/">judaicadh.github.io/morais-ledger</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its physical rescue and presence at Penn is entirely due to the vision
            and generosity of <strong>Marvin Weiner</strong>, the chairman of the
            library committee at Dropsie College, founded in 1907 and transformed in
            1986 into the Annenberg Research Institute, a post-graduate research
            center. Weiner discovered the Morais Ledger sometime during the early
            1950s while browsing Sam Kleinman&rsquo;s Schuylkill Book Shop, then
            located at the corner of Lancaster and Belmont in West Philadelphia, and
            purchased it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Over the course of the next four decades, Weiner cataloged onto index
            cards and cross-referenced each item in the ledger. On each index card,
            Weiner identified the work pasted in the Ledger and provided a
            transcription of Morais&rsquo;s handwritten annotations. He also compared
            the Ledger&rsquo;s contents with Moshe Davis&rsquo;s 1947 annotated
            bibliography of Morais&rsquo;s writings (Moshe Davis, &ldquo;Sabato
            Morais: Selected and Annotated Bibliography of His Writings,&rdquo; in
            <em>Publications of the American Jewish Historical Society</em> no. 37
            [1947], pp. 55&ndash;93) and noted each item Davis had not listed, which
            amounted to hundreds of otherwise unknown articles. To supplement the
            catalogue of the contents of the ledger and to provide better access to
            it, Weiner created a register of the newspapers in the Ledger,
            alphabetized by title and accompanied by the date of each issue from
            which an article had been clipped.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 1992, Weiner donated the Morais Ledger, as he named it, to the ARI. In
            1993, the ARI and its library merged with the University of Pennsylvania
            and was renamed the Center for Judaic Studies. In 1997, Weiner
            commissioned Leslie DeLauter, then working at the University of
            Pennsylvania Rare Book and Manuscript Library, to type his index card
            catalogue into a computer. The typing of the Marvin Weiner Catalogue of
            the Sabato Morais Ledger was the precondition for the digital publication
            of both.
          </p>
          <p>
            The final steps of editing, proofreading, formatting, and indexing the
            Catalogue were undertaken by <strong>Gina Glasman</strong>, a doctoral
            student at Columbia University, and <strong>Etty Lassman</strong>, a
            Research Assistant for the Fellowship program at what had been renamed
            the Center for Advanced Judaic Studies at the University of Pennsylvania
            (today known as the Herbert D. Katz Center for Advanced Judaic Studies at
            Penn). Glasman, who completed her work in 2001, served as editor of the
            project, compared the catalogue with the contents of the Ledger,
            established a uniform entry format, and created a name and subject index.
            Lassman completed the project, overseeing the proofreading and layout for
            the final product.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Herbert and Sheila Weiner</strong>, the son and daughter-in-law of
            Marvin and Sybil Weiner, funded the launching of the Morais transcription
            project. Their generous support was made in honor and memory of their
            parents. The contributions of these two generations of the Weiner family
            to save, preserve, make accessible, and transcribe the legacy of Sabato
            Morais will never be forgotten.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Transcription team -->
    <div class="mt-12">
      <section class="frame-gold rounded-sm bg-card p-7 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="mb-1 font-heading text-2xl text-navy">Transcription &amp; Review</h2>
        <p class="mb-6 font-sans text-sm text-ink-muted">
          A portion of Morais's writings and correspondence was transcribed and
          reviewed by volunteers on FromThePage; other transcriptions were generated
          with AI assistance (see our{" "}
          <a href="/methodology" class="text-burgundy underline">Methodology</a>).
          We are grateful to the following contributors.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-3">
          {transcribers.map((person) => (
            <li class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-body text-lg text-ink">
              <Motif class="shrink-0 translate-y-1 text-gold" size={13} />
              <span>
                {person.name}
                {person.role && (
                  <span class="block font-sans text-sm text-ink-muted">{person.role}</span>
                )}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <p class="mb-3 mt-7 font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
          Additional contributors, credited by username
        </p>
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {reviewers.map((name) => (
            <li class="rounded-full border border-border bg-paper-light px-4 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-ink">
              {name}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Partners -->
    <div class="mt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Partner Institutions</p>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {partners.map((p) => (
          <li class="border-b border-border py-2 font-body text-lg text-ink">{p}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Rights note -->
    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-border pt-8 text-center">
      <div class="ornament mx-auto mb-6 max-w-xs">
        <Motif class="text-gold" size={16} />
      </div>
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-2xl font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Materials are reproduced with the permission of the holding institutions.
        For questions about rights and reuse, or to suggest a correction, please
        contact{" "}
        <a href="https://judaicadhpenn.org/" class="text-burgundy underline">Judaica Digital Humanities at Penn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
